301
00:08:16,930 --> 00:08:18,660
Now agents do the production.

302
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:20,110
He gives the direction.

303
00:08:20,320 --> 00:08:21,540
So what's left when

304
00:08:21,580 --> 00:08:23,300
even the doing is gone?

305
00:08:24,710 --> 00:08:26,980
Number one isn't the hardest job.

306
00:08:27,020 --> 00:08:28,800
It's a different kind of job.

307
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:29,440
It's the one where

308
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:30,600
we want a human.

309
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:31,780
On purpose.

310
00:08:31,950 --> 00:08:32,790
Computers have beaten

311
00:08:32,830 --> 00:08:33,520
the best chess

312
00:08:33,560 --> 00:08:35,450
players for almost thirty years.

313
00:08:35,490 --> 00:08:37,610
And chess has never been bigger.

314
00:08:37,730 --> 00:08:39,110
About 10 million people play

315
00:08:39,150 --> 00:08:40,930
online every single day.

316
00:08:41,010 --> 00:08:42,500
Machines play each other too.

317
00:08:42,670 --> 00:08:44,980
The crowds come for the humans.

318
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:47,030
It's the person who sits

319
00:08:47,070 --> 00:08:48,840
with you when the news is bad.

320
00:08:49,170 --> 00:08:50,480
The one who signs off,

321
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:51,760
and answers for it.

322
00:08:51,970 --> 00:08:53,210
The one who decides what's

323
00:08:53,250 --> 00:08:55,220
worth making in the first place.

324
00:08:55,450 --> 00:08:56,310
Those aren't tasks

325
00:08:56,350 --> 00:08:57,720
a machine can't do.

326
00:08:57,910 --> 00:08:58,930
They're tasks we want

327
00:08:58,970 --> 00:09:00,210
a person to do.

328
00:09:00,580 --> 00:09:02,070
The last human job isn't

329
00:09:02,110 --> 00:09:03,760
the one machines can't do.

330
00:09:03,910 --> 00:09:06,040
It's the one we won't hand over.

331
00:09:07,400 --> 00:09:08,700
So how do you stay

332
00:09:08,740 --> 00:09:10,380
on the right side of the row?

333
00:09:10,610 --> 00:09:12,360
First, judgment.

334
00:09:12,420 --> 00:09:14,650
Telling good from merely finished.

335
00:09:14,690 --> 00:09:15,920
It's why companies still pay

336
00:09:15,960 --> 00:09:16,930
for the senior who can

337
00:09:16,970 --> 00:09:18,100
tell the difference.

338
00:09:18,140 --> 00:09:19,180
It protects you from being

339
00:09:19,220 --> 00:09:20,650
swapped for a button.

340
00:09:20,790 --> 00:09:22,510
Second, directing.

341
00:09:22,620 --> 00:09:24,250
Breaking a goal into steps,

342
00:09:24,290 --> 00:09:25,530
handing them to agents,

343
00:09:25,570 --> 00:09:27,030
checking what comes back.

344
00:09:27,120 --> 00:09:27,800
That's what Jakob

345
00:09:27,840 --> 00:09:29,220
does every day now.

346
00:09:29,260 --> 00:09:30,330
It protects you from being

347
00:09:30,370 --> 00:09:31,970
the task that gets automated,

348
00:09:32,010 --> 00:09:32,980
because you become

349
00:09:33,020 --> 00:09:34,320
the one who runs it.

350
00:09:34,980 --> 00:09:36,740
Third, trust.

351
00:09:36,990 --> 00:09:39,020
People still buy from people,

352
00:09:39,060 --> 00:09:41,420
hire people, follow people.

353
00:09:41,740 --> 00:09:42,960
Relationships protect

354
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:43,530
you from being

355
00:09:43,570 --> 00:09:45,790
compared on price with a machine.

356
00:09:46,030 --> 00:09:48,640
Fourth, hands plus a head.

357
00:09:48,860 --> 00:09:51,460
A trade, with AI in your pocket.

358
00:09:51,580 --> 00:09:53,360
It protects you because the robot

359
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:55,030
isn't in the basement yet.

360
00:09:55,150 --> 00:09:56,240
And when it arrives,

361
00:09:56,280 --> 00:09:57,890
someone has to run it.

362
00:09:58,610 --> 00:10:01,350
And fifth, learning in steps.

363
00:10:01,420 --> 00:10:03,270
Not one big retraining.

364
00:10:03,450 --> 00:10:04,480
One new step,

365
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:05,490
every time a model

366
00:10:05,530 --> 00:10:06,770
takes the old one.

367
00:10:06,900 --> 00:10:08,360
It protects you from waking up

368
00:10:08,400 --> 00:10:10,680
with a skill no one is hiring for.

369
00:10:10,920 --> 00:10:12,110
Even Bill Gates calls

370
00:10:12,150 --> 00:10:13,690
this a turbulent era.

371
00:10:13,760 --> 00:10:14,950
Which is exactly why

372
00:10:14,990 --> 00:10:16,250
the steps matter.

373
00:10:29,490 --> 00:10:30,520
Every time the machine

374
00:10:30,560 --> 00:10:31,710
took a step,

375
00:10:31,750 --> 00:10:33,410
the human took one up.

376
00:10:33,680 --> 00:10:35,540
So the last human job isn't

377
00:10:35,580 --> 00:10:37,310
waiting at the end of the row.

378
00:10:37,460 --> 00:10:39,530
It's the step you take next.

379
00:10:39,760 --> 00:10:41,950
And I think what's left for me

380
00:10:41,990 --> 00:10:43,880
right now is to decide what's

381
00:10:43,920 --> 00:10:45,730
worth making and why.

382
00:10:45,980 --> 00:10:47,060
This channel exists

383
00:10:47,100 --> 00:10:48,420
so that superintelligence

384
00:10:48,460 --> 00:10:50,150
goes well for everyone.

385
00:10:50,300 --> 00:10:51,300
Want that too?

386
00:10:51,340 --> 00:10:52,490
Then subscribe.

